&lt;h2 id="garden-description"&gt;Garden Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;According to Eschebach's plan, there was a &lt;em&gt;portico&lt;/em&gt; at the rear of this house that enclosed this &lt;em&gt;peristyle&lt;/em&gt; garden (a) on four sides. A small section of the foundation wall remains on the south end of the east side. The &lt;em&gt;cubiculum&lt;/em&gt; (b) to the east of the &lt;em&gt;atrium&lt;/em&gt; has a garden representation on the west half of the black &lt;em&gt;predella&lt;/em&gt; on the south wall. It was poorly preserved but the left section shows a garden with a lattice fence and a pergola. Faint images remain of a similar pergola on the right side. The center of the painting, (which is 0.09 x 0.84 m.) has an open area with a crater perhaps serving as a fountain in a pergola. Two additional pergolas stand to either side.&lt;/p&gt;
